    }
  ],
  "description": "Each operator alert is raised and cleared as an audit event (session model §11), alert_id matching the clear to its raise — which is how a restarted core rebuilds the active set from the log. An alert is TSB's own internal state, never host state (Contract §4): it names TSB's components — the supervisor, a worker, the sessions affected — and never a pid, a path or a hostname. It is bound to no principal. supervisor_unresponsive names its supervisor; worker_unkillable its worker and the supervisor that could not kill it.",
  "corpus": [
    "session model §11",
    "Contract §4",
    "Storage §6",
    "External_Study §1.3"
  ],
